\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10.1}{\ignorespaces The attribute schema, and the visual band each attribute is judged from. The region column is a manual routing table: a wrong entry is invisible at run time, because the evidence line still reads correctly but quotes the sharpness of the wrong part of the body.}}{104}{table.caption.110}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10.2}{\ignorespaces VLM noise on one track. A majority vote would report \texttt {hair\_color}${=}$black on a 40/30/30 split, and would break the 40/40 tie on \texttt {upper\_inner\_color} by whichever value the sort visited first.}}{106}{table.caption.111}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10.3}{\ignorespaces What the CLIP score separates \emph {inside} the 75-candidate pool. The AUC is the probability that a ground-truth crop outranks a non-ground-truth crop there; 1.0 would mean the score alone sorts the pool perfectly, and 0.5 would be chance. It is computed with ties taken into account, because many crops share the same similarity to three decimals and counting a tie as a win would overstate the score exactly where it is weakest.}}{115}{table.caption.122}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.1}{\ignorespaces Per-call token budget. Output excludes thinking tokens, which are billed as output and counted against the same rate window, so the real output load is higher than this column. The reliable signal for a truncated reply is the API's \texttt {finish\_reason}, not the reported output count.}}{119}{table.caption.126}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.2}{\ignorespaces 100 identities out of the 496-identity subset (Section~\ref {sec:r-dataset}), pool of 75 candidates, zero-shot, one descriptive phrasing each. At $n=100$ a percentage point is one identity.}}{120}{table.caption.129}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.3}{\ignorespaces Lost: inside CLIP's top 10, not in the funnel's. Rescued: outside CLIP's top 10, inside the funnel's. No pool: the ground truth was not among the 75 retrieved crops at all, so no reranking could have returned it.}}{121}{table.caption.130}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.4}{\ignorespaces The five identities CLIP had in its top 10 and the funnel did not return. `Stage 2' is the coarse round's rank out of the candidates it ranked; `n/a' in stage 4 means the refine round never saw that candidate.}}{122}{table.caption.131}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.5}{\ignorespaces The five lost identities re-ranked by a larger model at stages 2B and 4B only. `Stage 2' and `Stage 4' read \emph {before} $\rightarrow $ \emph {after}.}}{123}{table.caption.132}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11.6}{\ignorespaces What each mechanism changed, and how strong the evidence is.}}{128}{table.11.6}%
